# Smart Bookshelf API — ISBN lookup and import (VS Code "REST Client" extension).
# These requests call real external APIs (Google Books, then Open Library).
# Without GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY Google often answers 429, so data comes from Open Library.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lookup only (nothing is saved)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Look up by ISBN-13 (hyphens allowed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/978-0-13-235088-4

### Same book by ISBN-10 — normalized to ISBN-13, second call is served from cache (meta.cached = true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/0-13-235088-2

### Polish edition ("Ostatnie życzenie", Andrzej Sapkowski)
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/9788375780635

### 400 — invalid checksum
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/978-0-13-235088-5

### 404 — valid ISBN unknown to every source
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/9790000000001

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Import (lookup + save as a new book)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Import with fetched data only
# @name importBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "978-83-7578-063-5"
}

### Show the imported book
@importedId = {{importBook.response.body.data.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{importedId}}

### Delete the imported book (so the import above can be repeated)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{{importedId}}

### Import with overrides (any editable book field; tags replace fetched ones; rfidUid/locationStatus are rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "9780261103573",
  "status": "READING",
  "pagesRead": 40,
  "startedAt": "2026-11-24",
  "tags": ["fantasy", "classics"]
}

### Import into a free shelf slot (copy a slot id, e.g. slot 5 from the seed, via Prisma Studio)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "9788375780635",
  "slotId": "PASTE-SLOT-UUID-HERE"
}

### 409 — ISBN already in the library (Clean Code from the seed, given as ISBN-10)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "0-13-235088-2"
}

### 400 — invalid ISBN
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "123"
}

### 404 — ISBN unknown to every source
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/import
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "9790000000001"
}
